---
import { profile, claudeWork, sameSession } from "../data/profile";
---

<section id="claude" class="claude">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 · How this site was made</p>
      <h2>Claude Code built this page. I built the other one.</h2>
      <p>
        This site came from a single prompt. My hand-coded portfolio from 2021 is still online at{" "}
        <a href={profile.manmade}>manmade.farhantaufiks.com</a>. Same person, same CV, different
        tools. Compare them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="split">
      <figure class="prompt">
        <figcaption class="mono">prompt.txt: everything I specified</figcaption>
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            "Create a website to introduce myself, as Earth Science and Comp Science. That could be my
            whole tagline. I won't give you specific instructions. Base it on what I do, how I talk to
            you in other sessions, my background, my LinkedIn and my CV. Keep it separate from the
            current site, deployable on its own, in the same repo."
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <div class="decided">
          <p class="mono">What Claude decided on its own</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The stack: Astro, with no JavaScript framework shipped to the browser</li>
            <li>The concept: topographic hero, career as a stratigraphic column</li>
            <li>Every word of copy, the palette and the type</li>
            <li>The repo split: <code>manmade/</code> and <code>web/</code>, built and deployed independently</li>
            <li>The nginx vhosts, TLS and the deploy to my VPS</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <div class="notes">
        <h3>How I use it day to day</h3>
        <ul class="check">
          {claudeWork.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
        </ul>

        <h3>In the same session, before this page</h3>
        <ol class="log mono">
          {sameSession.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
        </ol>
        <p class="aside">
          The part I own: deciding what to build, checking what comes back, and saying no when it is
          wrong. The typing is the cheap part now.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .claude {
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 28px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .prompt {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  figcaption {
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  figcaption::before {
    content: "";
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--moss);
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 22px 22px 18px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .decided {
    padding: 18px 22px 22px;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule);
  }
  .decided .mono {
    color: var(--ochre);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .decided ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--moss);
  }
  .notes h3 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .notes h3:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }
  .check {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
  }
  .check li {
    padding-left: 24px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .check li::before {
    content: "▸";
    position: absolute;
    left: 4px;
    color: var(--ochre);
  }
  .log {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px 18px 16px 40px;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .log li::marker {
    color: var(--moss);
  }
  .aside {
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
